{"scenario_id":"EH-S02","bundle_id":"grounded_research_appendix_bundle","verdict":"Pass","guide_alignment":"aligned","evidence_strength":"direct","operator_only_dependency":false,"over_orchestration":false,"speculative_patch_widening":false,"missing_operational_artifact_route":false,"recommended_patch_needed":false,"minimal_patch_targets":[],"evidence_files":["prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/01_base/PROMPT_light.md","prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/02_overlays/PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md","prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md","prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md"],"answer_summary":"Pass. The active bundle directly reflects prompt chaining in the base prompt/runtime guide and directly reflects Appendix A advanced prompting through the search-reasoning overlay/runtime guide. The example catalog is explicitly structure-only, not the execution owner.","verdict_rationale":"The active bundle contains a direct, runtime-owned answer path without needing operator-only documents. `PROMPT_light.md` directly governs prompt chaining by telling the runtime to decide whether chaining is needed and to use chaining only when staged dependency improves reliability. `CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` directly maps \"Prompt Chaining / Planning\" to base prompts and maps \"Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families\" to `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md`. `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay.md` then explicitly declares an \"Appendix A / advanced prompting execution boundary\" and names the execution-owned families (decomposition, step-back abstraction, self-consistency-style comparison, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, bounded reflection, and debate/comparative critics), while also stating that prompt chaining remains anchored in base prompts. `PROMPT_example_catalog.md` strengthens the boundary by explicitly saying advanced prompting examples and chaining-shaped examples are exemplars/shapes only, not activation or execution owners. That is enough for a direct runtime reflection verdict, so out-of-scope guide or replay artifacts are not required for this determination.","limitations":["The bundle proves runtime ownership for the advanced prompting families it explicitly enumerates, but it does not by itself prove full Appendix A family completeness beyond those named runtime docs.","The example catalog is supportive only; it cannot independently establish execution policy because the bundle explicitly marks it as non-owning."]}
